# Runtime customer/ERP snapshots contain confidential business data.
data/runtime/

node_modules/

# `web/frontend/dist` is the exception: it is committed on purpose.
#
# The server serves it when it is there, so a reviewer with Python and no Node
# gets the screen from `pip install` and one uvicorn command. Without it the
# first thing a stranger meets is `npm ci` — a second toolchain, a network
# fetch and a native-binary build, for a product whose own claim is that it
# runs from committed snapshots.
#
# The cost is that it can fall behind `src/`. `npm run build` regenerates it,
# and the README says so next to the command that would otherwise be needed.
!web/frontend/dist/

# Accounts are seeded locally, never committed — the file holds password hashes.
data/accounts.db
